    "uncertainCells": [],
    "notes": "ORIGINAL PRINTING: the typewriter-style, one-sided 1964 Virdon card (left-hand card of the 1600x1406 scan; the right-hand card is the modern-typeface reissue transcribed as batter_virdon-bill_1964). It differs from the modern printing in its ratings (stealing-D here, stealing-E on the modern card), in its record (WALKS 29 here, BB 30 on the modern card), and in a different grid arrangement: e.g. this card prints its two WALKs at col2 r8 and r12 (modern: col1 r5 and col3 r3) and its TRIPLE 1 / SINGLE** split at col3 r6 (modern: TRIPLE 1-2 at col3 r9). Neither printing has a HOMERUN result (3 HR in 1964). Source: a 2019 collector's post of his Bill Virdon Strat-O-Matic cards (Wayback capture). Read from 1.1x half-card crops, then a second independent pass over a 1.0x crop of the whole grid. 'outs as pos- sible' is line-wrap hyphenation, recorded as 'into as many outs as possible'. Col2 roll2 prints 'plus injury' under 'lineout (2b)'. 1964 BATTING RECORD box lists the seven stats AT BATS, DOUBLES, TRIPLES, HOMERUNS, AVERAGE, WALKS, STRIKEOUTS."
